course: dictionary
lesson: 5844
title: Malaria: an illness spread by mosquitoes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Malaria is a serious illness. It gives you a high fever, shivering and sweating, and it can kill you if nobody treats it.
explain: You cannot catch malaria from a cough or a hug. It is caused by a tiny parasite, which is a living thing too small to see. The parasite gets into your blood when an infected mosquito bites you.
explain: «Some mosquitoes carry malaria, which kills about 600,000 people a year, mostly young children in Africa.» That is why mosquitoes are among the deadliest animals to people.
explain: Malaria is most common in hot, wet places. People stay safe with bed nets, insect spray, draining still water where mosquitoes lay eggs, and anti-malaria tablets for travellers.
fact: Malaria means a serious illness with high fever, shivering and sweating.
fact: Malaria is caused by a tiny parasite that gets into the blood through a mosquito bite.
fact: «Fever trees» are real yellow-barked trees of wet ground, named long ago because people near them caught fever.
fact: Tu Youyou won the 2015 Nobel Prize for artemisinin, a malaria drug from sweet wormwood.
fact: Malaria is a good example of a disease spread by an animal, the mosquito.
exercise: «Malaria causes high fever, shivering and sweating.» What do these clues tell you about malaria? | It is a kind of cold weather | *It is an illness that makes you very hot and shaky | It is a sweet fruit | It is a type of shark
exercise: «Some mosquitoes carry malaria, which kills about 600,000 people a year.» What can malaria do to people? | Turn them into birds | *Kill them if it is not treated | Make them taller | Make them sneeze
exercise: Which of these is NOT a way to stay safe from malaria? | Taking anti-malaria tablets when travelling | *Leaving still water where mosquitoes can lay eggs | Using insect spray | Sleeping under a bed net
test: What kind of illness is malaria? | A cold that goes away in a day | A sort of sweet fruit | A type of bird | *A serious illness that can kill if it is not treated
test: How is malaria spread from one person to another? | Through the air, like a cold | By touching hands | By drinking dirty water only | *By an infected mosquito biting a person and passing on the parasite
exam: Why are mosquitoes called some of the deadliest animals to people? | Because they live on the tops of mountains | Because they are the biggest animals in Africa | *Because some carry malaria, which kills many people every year | Because they bite very loudly
